+      "html": "<p>This briefing raises <strong>no new methodology flags</strong>. It is a transparency exercise that explains an existing published composite with direct evidence, and every dimension reconstructs to the canonical formula at 0.0 drift. The published United States score, <strong>17.5 / 100, Critical, rank 152</strong>, is presented unchanged. No score change is proposed or implied. The observation worth recording for future reflection, not as a flag but as a note, is that the United States is a clean illustration of the near-floor accountability logic already documented in the &quot;State of Exception&quot; briefing: a mid-Critical score held above the floor precisely by the surviving remediation surface, and therefore highly sensitive to whether that surface is preserved or removed.</p>\n<p>Independence statement: entities never pay for inclusion, score changes, or suppression of findings. This briefing interprets the existing record against current public evidence. It measures the conduct of the state, not any party or administration.</p>\n<hr>"
